#
# The stock of a product after a sale, in Sutra (mercer_rules.h MR1): what
# was on the shelf less what was sold, in whole units, never below zero.
# stock, sold and left fit 9(9): a sale of more than the stock makes left
# negative, a size error, refused; once (sold - 1) is unsigned, so a sale
# of no unit is refused too. stock.kron answers any stock past nine
# digits: past 9(9) the two disagree, held.
record stock-after-sale
  stock: 9(9)
  sold: 9(9)
  once: 9(9)
  left: 9(9)
procedure
  compute once = sold - 1
  compute left = stock - sold
  answer left
